[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_page")
id = &"winning"
title = "Winning and losing"
order = 120
summary = "Elimination needs both your army and your buildings gone."
body = "You are ELIMINATED when you have no living squads AND no living buildings.
Either one alone keeps you in.

That cuts both ways. A player with one gatherer crew and no town can found
another and carry on. And a base razed to nothing while the army is still in
the field has cost its owner an economy, not a match.

The match ends when one player — or one team — is the last left standing.

## So razing is not enough

Take the buildings and the troops. Whichever you leave is what they rebuild
from.

## Leaving, and being cut off

Leaving a match returns you to the lobby, and it leaves nothing behind:
every squad AND every building you own is removed the moment you go, so
by the rule above you are eliminated at once. There is nothing special
about quitting — it is the ordinary rule applied to a player who no
longer has anything.

## Conceding

If you are beaten and would rather not be chased down, you can concede.
It razes what you own, so the same rule notices on the next tick and the
match can end — which is the point: a lost position should not cost
everybody else another twenty minutes.

If you were HOSTING, the match ends for everybody. A hosted game runs inside
the host's own client, so there is nothing left to play on."
sources = Array[String](["res://match_state.gd", "res://decisions/D-027.md", "res://decisions/D-075-leaving-a-match-returns-to-the.md"])
stamp = "6e5cdad0224107dbb0869c4ca0178a9bdcb3760ed054c47291af79c9ba2b3c75"
